{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I.</b> Some say it is inverted, like גוער (rebuking). Others say it means מניח (causing to rest), after its waves roared — like מרגוע (Jeremiah 6:16) — and this is correct in my eyes. Or its meaning is: I cause the sea to rest, and I command that its waves roar. The sense is a parable about the oppressors."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:03.058670903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}